+# Patch 0065: Show rebuilt as an animated UI demonstration, and the false "card payment waiting" error
+
+This patch applies on top of 0064 (the grid fit). Apply 0064 first.
+
+## What you asked for
+1. The **Show** stage should work like the explanatory document: a polished, user-paced, animated demonstration of a process using representations of the app's screens, with zooms, pans, transitions, simulated taps, toggles, spotlights and guidance text. Watched, not practised. Not a literal spec, so use judgement.
+2. Starting **Guide** said "A card payment is still waiting on the reader" when nothing was waiting.
+3. Update the spec docs to reflect the clarification.
+
+## What was wrong with the error (2)
+`trainingBlocker` refused to start practice if **any** card attempt anywhere in the history had the status `started` or `unknown`, with no time limit. An attempt is left at `started` whenever the app is closed or loses the iPad mid-payment, and nothing ever clears it, so one such attempt blocked training for good. Now:
+- `started` only blocks for 5 minutes after it began (the same window the screensaver and staff lock already use for "a payment is in flight").
+- `unknown` only blocks while its sale is still the one in the cart. For any other sale there is nothing you could finish from here.
+- A part-paid cart still blocks, as before.
+- The messages now say which case it is.
+
+## How Show works now (1)
+- **Mock screens in a canvas.** A demo is one or more screens made of simple nodes (panel, bar, text, button, tile, row, toggle, field, chip, icon) placed in a fixed canvas, drawn in the app's own colours so it looks like the till. The welcome course's Show is a mock Checkout with the Guide dock, then a "Course complete" screen.
+- **Camera.** It zooms in on the control a step is about (up to 2.2 times, picked automatically to fit unless the step says otherwise), pans, and never slides past the canvas edge.
+- **Pointer.** A pointer glides to a control and taps it with a ripple, a small press on the control and a tick.
+- **The screen responds.** After the tap, nodes appear, disappear, change text, flip a toggle or take a highlight, and a change of screen is a cross-fade.
+- **Spotlight and notes.** The picture dims around the ringed control (same amber ring as Guide), and a short note with an arrow sits beside it.
+- **Your pace.** Each step plays once when it opens and then waits. **Next**, **Back** and **Replay** are the only ways it moves. There is no autoplay, no Pause, and no "watch it through first" gate. Going Back or jumping shows the finished picture straight away. If the iPad's Reduce Motion setting is on, the movement is skipped and each step just appears.
+- **Order inside a step:** camera to the target, pointer taps, the screen changes, camera settles and the note appears.
+- **Authoring.** `validateModule` now checks every Show: ids, screens, nodes that fit the canvas, a `tap` on something that is not on screen at that moment, a `focus` that is not on screen afterwards, missing icons, zoom limits. The old Show format (icons sliding about) is gone. Info keeps its slideshow.
+
+## Files
+- New: `src/lib/trainingDemo.ts` (pure: state after each step, camera, step plan, note placement, checker), `src/ui/DemoView.tsx` (drawing and animation), `tests/trainingdemo.test.ts`.
+- Changed: `src/lib/trainingModule.ts` (the `Demo` types, `show: Demo`, checker), `src/lib/trainingSandbox.ts` (the blocker), `src/screens/TrainingRun.tsx` (Info slideshow and the new Show runner; autoplay removed), `src/lib/trainingScene.ts` (dead autoplay timing removed), `src/training/modules/welcome.ts` (new Show), `tests/training.test.ts`, `tests/trainingspots.test.ts`, `tests/trainingsandbox.test.ts`.
+- Docs: `DEV_NOTES.md` item 6 (your Show clause, with the clarification), `docs/PROGRESS.md` (B6 text and patch log row), `src/training/README.md` (new "Writing a Show" section), `help/staff/training.md` and `help/help.json`, `docs/next-steps.html`.
+
+## Steps
+1. [x] Re-fetched the repo (HEAD "Fixed Tab Bar & Worker Migration") and stacked this on 0064.
+2. [x] Fixed the blocker, with tests for each case (fresh, old, other sale, same sale, part-paid).
+3. [x] Pure demo engine and its tests (camera limits, step plans, note placement, every checker rule, and a test that every course Show taps, changes and directs the eye).
+4. [x] `DemoView` and the Show runner.
+5. [x] Welcome course Show rewritten as a real demonstration.
+6. [x] Spec docs updated. 31 training tests, plus the help tests, pass. `tsc` reports nothing for the files I changed.
+7. [ ] You: run it on the iPad. I could not run the animation here, only the logic around it, so please check: smoothness, that the zoomed text is sharp enough (the canvas is scaled, so very large zooms can look soft; the cap is 2.2 times), the pointer and ring landing on the right controls, Replay, and Reduce Motion.
+
+## Things to know
+- DEV_NOTES.md was edited, at your request: only the Show clause in item 6, keeping your wording and adding the clarification. Please take the new version if you keep your own copy.
+- Task courses you add later each need their own Show: a mock of the real screens for that job (tiles, sheets, keypad and so on), written with the node kinds above. If a screen needs a control the node kinds do not cover, add a kind rather than faking it.
+- Still open from before: an attempt left at `started` is never cleaned up (it just stops mattering after 5 minutes). Nothing needs it cleaned, but the attempts list in Support & diagnostics will keep showing it as started.
